# Comments only when tricky

Keep a comment only when a careful human reader would otherwise miss a non-obvious **why** (invariant, hazard, workaround, intentional asymmetry).

## Do

- Prefer names and structure so most code needs no comment.
- After a refactor or simplification, delete comments that no longer earn their place (legacy notes, narrating JSDoc, restated types).
- One short line when needed; explain the why, not the what.

## Do not

- Comment every export, helper, or obvious control flow.
- Leave migration / “for later tickets” comments after that context is gone.
- Add comments “for the agent” that a human would not need.
